From 48beb3bee54defa4989ec6ef211fa630ef5c9972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:50:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve Windows executable extensions in Bazel tests

Forward the native client's PATHEXT alongside SYSTEMROOT, COMSPEC, and
WINDIR. Extensionless executable discovery uses this environment input;
Bazel's sanitized test environment otherwise drops it.

Existing native regression: cli-doctor_path_safety-test fails to discover
the git.cmd fixture with which8, while retaining the no-helper-execution
assertions. run38747669404 job116473691446 records eight passing cases and
this one failing discovery assertion in bazel-msvc-271217d.log. Windows
execution with the restored environment remains a hosted acceptance gate.

This configuration repair does not change product lookup semantics or relax
the diagnostic safety assertions. Base rust-v0.162.1 with the preceding
issue-61 queue through zzzz-0018.
---
 .bazelrc                                 | 2 ++
 codex-rs/cli/tests/doctor_path_safety.rs | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.bazelrc b/.bazelrc
index 1abee8dd0..31aa47c0f 100644
--- a/.bazelrc
+++ b/.bazelrc
@@ -56,6 +56,8 @@ common:macos --strategy=CcConfigureMakeRule=remote,sandboxed,local
 common:windows --test_env=SYSTEMROOT
 common:windows --test_env=COMSPEC
 common:windows --test_env=WINDIR
+# Windows executable discovery uses PATHEXT when resolving extensionless names.
+common:windows --test_env=PATHEXT
 # Rust's libtest harness runs test bodies on std-spawned threads. The default
 # 2 MiB stack can be too small for large async test futures on Windows CI; see
 # https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/19067 for the motivating failure.
diff --git a/codex-rs/cli/tests/doctor_path_safety.rs b/codex-rs/cli/tests/doctor_path_safety.rs
index bbc4f9f7b..34d749762 100644
--- a/codex-rs/cli/tests/doctor_path_safety.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/cli/tests/doctor_path_safety.rs
@@ -186,7 +186,9 @@ fn startup_and_doctor_do_not_execute_path_helpers() -> Result<()> {
         );
         assert_eq!(
             report["checks"]["git.environment"]["summary"],
-            "git executable found; execution not verified"
+            "git executable found; execution not verified",
+            "extensionless helper discovery uses PATHEXT on Windows: {:?}",
+            std::env::var_os("PATHEXT")
         );
         assert!(!fixture.marker.exists(), "doctor executed a PATH helper");
     }
